      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:kjkjgq'
    '|b||Percentage points are not percent. In the nudge-unit trials, about seventeen in a hundred acted without the nudge.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7480
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||So one point four points is a rise of about eight percent.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3920
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:x1vt2d'
    '|b||In the journals the base was about twenty-six, so eight point seven points is a rise of about a third.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6160
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:h74f21'
    '|a||So nudges are small and cheap. Should a government use them on us? I''ll argue yes.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6440
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||And I''ll argue we should be wary: a nudge can be manipulation.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4120
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1iab6k'
    '|a||My case: someone designs the counter anyway. Better on purpose and in the open, aimed at what people themselves want, with every option kept.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:nvz3ga'
    '|b||My case: a nudge often works because we don''t notice it. It goes around your reasoning instead of through it; philosophers like Daniel Hausman and Brynn Welch pressed exactly that.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12080
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:81k1g1'
    '|a||That part we can test. In a 2015 experiment, people were told up front which answer was ticked by default, and the default still worked about as well.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:v4qv3v'
    '|b||Fair. Then who nudges the nudgers? Officials have biases too: in one experiment, World Bank and British aid staff read the same data differently depending on their politics.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11880
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:sazxxk'
    '|b||And the state fails through what it can''t know and what it''s paid to want. A nudge escapes neither.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6880
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1edwm6v'
    '|a||Granted. Edward Glaeser''s point stings: a tax sits in the budget for everyone to fight over, a quiet nudge is harder to watch.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:bkz59w'
    '|a||That''s why Thaler and Sunstein say: never nudge in a way you couldn''t defend in public.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1edehx2'
    '|b||How sure are we? That nudges work a little, at scale: mostly agreed.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7320
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1qzzbgt'
    '|a||Whether steering people by their own lights respects them or manipulates them: contested. The data can''t settle that one.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1uqhs8k'
    '|b||Three new cases. A town wants fewer cars in its centre. Which of these is a nudge?':
